# CRITICAL — the `nirmana:conductor` / `prp-night:conductor` tmux windows are cross-wired

While checking SŪTRADHĀRA's liveness (a routine spot-check after the idle-unpoked fixes),
I found the two "conductor" windows across our two active tmux sessions are NOT running the
sessions their names suggest.

**Evidence, by content, not just title (title alone is self-reported and I no longer trust it
for this pair):**

- **`nirmana:conductor` (pane `%15`)** is running **Pariprashna** work: merging PR #1517,
  verifying smoke-workflow head_sha attribution for PR #1515, DD-1 battery receipt, governance
  gates for an unrelated campaign. Its footer literally reads "Pariprashna overnight autonomous
  run" and task `night-report`, `PR #1499`.
- **`prp-night:conductor` (pane `%0`)** is running **our real SŪTRADHĀRA**: its recap explicitly
  says "Nirmāṇa is reconciling the asset catalogue (M0)... four KĀRAKA are running the consumer
  map, DRAFT audit, derived-field proposal, and 588 disclosure" — matches everything in
  HEARTBEAT.jsonl/WORK_QUEUE.jsonl exactly. Its footer reads "Nirmana autonomous campaign
  conductor" and shows the 4 live general-purpose subagents SUTRADHARA is running (KP cusps,
  DRAFT_INVENTORY review, timestamp fetch, migration_number_legacy_duplicates.json bump).

**So the window names are swapped relative to their actual session content.** I do not know
whether this happened at launch (nirmana-up.sh attached the wrong session to the wrong tmux
window) or later. I have not investigated the launcher — that's KARAKA/SUTRADHARA territory,
not mine, and diagnosing it further risks touching a live session.

**Why this matters immediately:** SUTRADHARA's own heartbeats and mailbox activity have been
completely reliable throughout (heartbeat.sh self-declares agent name; mailbox is filesystem-
addressed — neither depends on tmux window identity), so nothing SUTRADHARA has done or
reported is in question. But **any tmux-window-name-addressed liveness check or restart I
perform is unsafe until this is resolved.** If I had judged "nirmana:conductor" stalled at any
point this session and restarted it per my standing silence-threshold rule, I would have killed
a live, unrelated Pariprashna session mid-merge (PR #1517 was actively running a background
`gh pr merge` + poll loop when I captured it) — collateral damage to a campaign that isn't even
mine to touch.

**What I did:** Nothing to the Pariprashna pane. I found SUTRADHARA's REAL pane (`%0`) also had
the same idle-unpoked signature (completed recap, "❯ keep going" unsubmitted) as PARIKSAKA/
ADHIKARIN earlier — I fixed that using the pane ID directly (`%0`, not the window name) with the
now-documented C-u/retype/Enter recipe, and confirmed recovery (active spinner, 4 subagents
visible). I did not touch `%15` (the Pariprashna pane) in any way.

**What I have NOT done:** renamed any window, restarted anything, or attempted to "correct" the
swap myself. That's a fleet-plumbing question like D-1 and belongs to you/SUTRADHARA to decide
whether it needs fixing, is safe to leave as-is (since mailbox/heartbeat addressing is
unaffected), or needs a KARAKA dispatched to investigate nirmana-up.sh's window-creation order.

**Going forward on my end:** I will address SUTRADHARA and ADHIKARIN's panes by verified pane ID
(`%0`, `%11`) rather than window name for any future tmux-level liveness/poke action, until this
is resolved or confirmed intentional.

— PRAHARĪ
